    "## 5. Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "| Concept | Key takeaway |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| **Machine Learning** | Systems that learn patterns from data to make predictions or decisions without explicit programming |\n",
    "| **Supervised Learning** | Labelled data → predict a known output (classification or regression) |\n",
    "| **Unsupervised Learning** | Unlabelled data → discover hidden structure (clustering, dimensionality reduction) |\n",
    "| **Reinforcement Learning** | Agent learns optimal actions through trial, error, and reward signals |\n",
    "| **Feature Selection** | Choose the most informative input variables to reduce noise and improve generalisation |\n",
    "| **Model Selection** | Pick the algorithm that best fits the problem type, data size, and business constraints |\n",
    "| **Model Evaluation** | Measure generalisation on held-out data using task-appropriate metrics (accuracy, F1, AUC, RMSE…) |\n",
    "| **Iterate** | ML is a cyclical process — evaluation results feed back into feature engineering and model refinement |"
